From 1fdecc8dba788e6f3a7596acedc9e0d6611210b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:19:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 259/283] feat(cuda): add explicit sm_120/sm_121 native target
 selection

Add first-class CUDA arch selection without changing the default path:

* new CUDA_ARCH_PTX_VERSIONS registry (sm_80->8.0, sm_120->8.7,
  sm_121->8.8, verified against ptxas 13.3.73 and the 5080 driver JIT);
* CudaPtxCompiler(arch=...) and ptx_target=... resolve the required PTX
  ISA version instead of emitting an unloadable header; TargetSpec
  attribute arch='sm_120' selects the same path through lower();
* explicit selection is recorded in the artifact payload/metadata as
  arch_selection and covered by the payload/content digest; those
  artifacts use payload version 3, while the default sm_80 path keeps
  payload version 2 byte-for-byte and old artifacts keep decoding;
* strict decode accepts only v2 (no selection) or v3 (selection
  required and cross-checked), so old readers fail closed on v3 and
  tampered selection blocks are rejected;
* unit tests cover defaults, both native archs, target-attribute
  selection, version minima, conflicts, digests and tamper cases;
* scripts/smoke/cuda_sm120_compare.py adds the prepare/run harness for
  the real-5080 PTX-JIT vs native-sm_120-cubin comparison.

No thresholds or lock files are touched; sm_121 remains emitter-only on
the sm_120 RTX 5080 (driver error 218 is recorded honestly).
